<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>MT 103 to MX address mapping</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Messages</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">MT 103 to MX address mapping</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>MT-to-MX address mapping</strong> is the rule set for converting party addresses between the legacy SWIFT MT format and ISO 20022. End-party addresses (Debtor, Creditor) map to MT fields using <strong>Option F</strong>; agent addresses use <strong>Option D</strong>. In MT 101 ingestion, the structured Option F sub-fields (50F, 59F) must carry Town Name and Country — free-text Option K is not acceptable as the sole carrier.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How MT 103 to MX address mapping works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>Mapping Scheme 1 governs the MX→MT direction with sub-field rules for Option F. Post-cutover, a bank cannot reliably derive <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> from Option K free text, so the resulting ISO 20022 message fails point-of-entry validation — corporates still on Option K should migrate to Option F before 15 November 2026.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §19.1–§19.6 (Mapping Scheme 1; Table 47 — Option F sub-field mapping); Swift, Removal of unstructured address.11 / pp.1-16 to 1-18.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
